itle":"Āmāra jīvana"}}},"song":{"meta":{"page":186,"first_line":"ātma-nivedana, tuyā pade kori","author":"Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur"},"title":["Ātma-nivedana"],"author":["by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur"],"verses":[{"number":"1","text":["ātma-nivedana,    tuyā pade kori,","    hoinu parama sukhī","duḥkha dūre gelo,    chintā nā rohilo,","    chaudike ānanda dekhi"],"translation":["I have become supremely joyful by surrendering myself at Your holy feet. Unhappiness has gone away, and there are no more anxieties. I see joy in all directions."],"isLong":false},{"number":"2","text":["aśoka-abhaya,    amṛta-ādhāra,","    tomāra charaṇa-dvaya","tāhāte ekhona,    viśrāma lobhiyā","    chāḍinu bhavera bhaya"],"translation":["Your two lotus feet are reservoirs of immortal nectar where one may live free from sorrow and fear. I have found peace there now and have given up the fear of worldly existence."],"isLong":false},{"number":"3","text":["tomāra saṁsāre,    koribo sevana,","    nahibo phalera bhāgī","tava sukha jāhe,    koribo jatana,","    ho’ye pade anurāgī"],"translation":["I shall render service in Your household and not endeavour to enjoy the fruits of that service, but rather I shall strive for whatever pleases You, fully devoted to Your lotus feet."],"isLong":false},{"number":"4","text":["tomāra sevāya,    duḥkha hoya jato,","    seo to’ parama sukha","sevā-sukha-duḥkha,    parama sampada","    nāśoye avidyā-duḥkha"],"translation":["Troubles encountered in Your service shall be the cause of great happiness, for in Your devotional service joy and sorrow are equally great riches. Both destroy the misery of ignorance."],"isLong":false},{"number":"5","text":["pūrva itihāsa,    bhulinu sakala,","    sevā-sukha pe’ye mane","āmi to’ tomāra,    tumi to’ āmāra,","    ki kāja apara dhane"],"translation":["I have completely forgotten all past history by feeling great joy in my mind. I am most certainly Yours, and You are indeed mine. What need is there of any other treasure?"],"isLong":false},{"number":"6","text":["bhakativinoda,    ānande ḍubiyā,","    tomāra sevāra tore","saba cheṣṭā kore,    tava ichā-mata,","    thākiyā tomāra ghore"],"translation":["Bhakti Vinod, diving into the ocean of bliss, devotes all his efforts for Your service and dwells in Your house according to Your wishes."],"isLong":false}],"resources":{"audio":[{"title":"Kamal Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/jayasri-sound/16-atma-nivedana","personSlug":"kamal-krishna-prabhu"},{"title":"Manasa Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/huron/atma-nivedana","personSlug":"manasa-krishna-prabhu"}]},"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":false,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":null},"head":{"canonical":"/en-2022/atma-nivedana-tuya-pade-kori/","description":"Ātma-nivedana — a Vaiṣṇava song by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Kirtan Guide.","title":"Ātma-nivedana. by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en-2022","slug":"atma-nivedana-tuya-pade-kori"}}